From: Tribuchet contributors
Subject: [PATCH] external builders: hand the build's timeouts to the builder

An external builder runs the build elsewhere, as a remote builder does,
and only it can tell the build's running time from the time it waits
or is held stopped. Write `timeout` and `maxSilentTime` into build.json
and leave them to the external builder, as Nix leaves them to a remote
builder: do not count them against the external builder's wall time.

diff --git a/src/libstore/build/derivation-building-goal.cc b/src/libstore/build/derivation-building-goal.cc
index 295f986258..8aab0433ea 100644
--- a/src/libstore/build/derivation-building-goal.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/build/derivation-building-goal.cc
@@ -1020,7 +1020,9 @@ Goal::Co DerivationBuildingGoal::buildLocally(
 
     actLock.reset();
 
-    worker.childStarted(shared_from_this(), {builderOut}, true, true);
+    /* An external builder gets the build's timeouts in build.json and
+       enforces them itself, as a remote builder does. */
+    worker.childStarted(shared_from_this(), {builderOut}, true, !localBuildCap.externalBuilder);
 
     started();
 
diff --git a/src/libstore/unix/build/external-derivation-builder.cc b/src/libstore/unix/build/external-derivation-builder.cc
index fc5358a1b8..7241c8307e 100644
--- a/src/libstore/unix/build/external-derivation-builder.cc
+++ b/src/libstore/unix/build/external-derivation-builder.cc
@@ -67,6 +67,8 @@ struct ExternalDerivationBuilder : DerivationBuilderImpl
         json.emplace("storeDir", store.storeDir);
         json.emplace("realStoreDir", store.config->realStoreDir.get());
         json.emplace("system", drv.platform);
+        json.emplace("timeout", settings.getWorkerSettings().buildTimeout.get());
+        json.emplace("maxSilentTime", settings.getWorkerSettings().maxSilentTime.get());
         {
             auto l = nlohmann::json::array();
             for (auto & i : inputPaths)
